definition {
    The indexer should live in the [core_analysis] module.
    On-disk schema: [sqlite_schema.ideas_index_sqlite] and [diagnostics_schema.diagnostics_sqlite].
    Layout and WAL sidecars: [sidecars.reqlan_directory_layout].
    Consumers: [consumers.index_consumers] (extends [consumption]).
    Sequencing and triggers: [sequencing.index_sequencing] (extends [triggers]).
    Cache reuse opportunities: [cache_reuse.index_cache_reuse].
}

index {
    The ideas graph indexer: parse `.rq` with the native engine, extract ideas/edges, persist to rusqlite SQLite.
    Same-file `[ideaset.member]` edges target the member leaf (["../language/syntax.rq".references_to_subidea]).
    Wildcard path+idea fan-out: [wildcard_reference_edges]
    (["../language/imports.rq".wildcard_references]).
    Ideas Summary graph can hide those edges via [ideas_summary_doc] /
    ["../extension/module/ideas_summary/graphical_graph.rq".wildcard_refs_toggle].
    Soft mtime sync skips unchanged files. `extract_version` in the ideas index meta is the extract-rule generation. When that number does not match the engine, sync rebuilds so stale edges do not remain (["../language/syntax.rq".inline_code]).
    Owned by [ownership]; consumed per [consumption].
    @tests (
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/tests/schema.rs:opens_at_schema_version_4"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/tests/schema.rs:schema_v4_columns_round_trip_git_count_and_mtime"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/tests/wildcard_reference_edges.rs:sync_persists_wildcard_reference_edges"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/tests/extract_parity.rs:qualified_ideaset_member_reference_targets_leaf_idea_not_ideaset"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/tests/broken_references.rs:sync_drops_stale_inline_code_file_refs_when_extract_version_changes"]
    )
}

wildcard_reference_edges {
    Native extract (`["../../crates/reqlan-index/src/extract.rs"]`) expands each AST wildcard
    against the idea catalog (`match_wildcard` / workspace candidate list).
    Persist one edge of kind `wildcard_reference` per matching idea (label = target idea name);
    never emit plain `references` for wildcard forms.
    Zero matches → one unresolved edge of the same kind (`isResolved: false`, label = pattern text).
    Edge ids use `edgeId(source, 'wildcard_reference', targetOrUnresolvedKey)`.
    Sync walks sorted `.rq` files and grows the catalog as it goes, so a wildcard file is
    expanded against ideas already stored plus files earlier in that walk
    (["../../crates/reqlan-index/src/sync.rs"]).
    Ancestor / reference-chain walks treat `wildcard_reference` like `references`
    (["../../packages/analytical/src/index-store/sqlite-store.ts"]).
    Ideas Summary references table groups them under sub-idea with other idea-to-idea links;
    graph visibility is [ideas_summary_doc] /
    ["../extension/module/ideas_summary/graphical_graph.rq".wildcard_refs_toggle].
    Soft mtime sync skips unchanged files — after introducing this edge kind, reindex (or touch)
    `.rq` files that contain wildcards so stored rows leave any legacy `references` fan-out.
    Langium `idea-extractor` keeps the same kind for remaining TS extract paths.
    Open-file local extract ([local_symbolic_analysis]) does not expand wildcards against a catalog.

    Related: ["../language/imports.rq".wildcard_references], [index], [indexer_rust],
    ["../extension/module/ideas_summary/graphical_graph.rq".wildcard_refs_toggle],
    [local_symbolic_analysis].

    @status done
    @implementation (
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/src/extract.rs"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/src/types.rs"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/src/sync.rs"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/src/extract.rs"]
        ["../../packages/analytical/src/core/types.ts"]
        ["../../packages/analytical/src/index-store/sqlite-store.ts"]
        ["../../packages/language/src/reqlan-wildcard-resolve.ts"]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/tests/wildcard_reference_edges.rs"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/tests/wildcard_reference_edges.rs:expands_wildcard_refs_to_one_edge_per_matching_idea"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/tests/wildcard_reference_edges.rs:emits_unresolved_edge_when_catalog_has_no_matches"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/tests/wildcard_reference_edges.rs:stores_wildcard_fan_out_as_wildcard_reference_kind"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/tests/wildcard_reference_edges.rs:extract_indexed_document_fans_out_edges_for_matching_catalog_ideas"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/tests/wildcard_reference_edges.rs:sync_persists_wildcard_reference_edges"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/tests/wildcard_reference_edges.rs:sync_persists_unresolved_wildcard_edge_when_catalog_has_no_matches"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/tests/wildcard_reference_edges.rs:indexer_and_graphical_graph_rq_capture_wildcard_edge_and_toggle_ideas"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/tests/wildcard_reference_edges.rs:stores_wildcard_fan_out_as_wildcard_reference_kind"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-export/tests/html_export.rs:html_export_workspace_graph_includes_wildcard_refs_chip_and_edges"]
    )
}

local_symbolic_analysis {
    Open-file symbolic analysis must run in Rust on one file only.
    Input: file URI plus source text (and optional import-root mappings).
    Output: ideas in that file, outbound edges with source byte spans, and same-file
    inbound backlinks (edges whose target is an idea declared in this file).
    Cross-file inbound still comes from SQLite via ["./cache-reuse.rq".unify_inbound_indexes].
    Do not read SQLite. Do not walk other workspace documents. Do not load an idea catalog.
    The language server confirms cross-file idea names with a separate depth-1 neighbor parse
    (["../extension/language-support/open-file-sequencing.rq".outbound_one_hop]).
    That hop is not part of this native extract.
    Wildcard forms stay one `wildcard_reference` pattern edge (unresolved); sync still expands
    them later via [wildcard_reference_edges].
    Flag: `ExtractOptions.local_symbolic` forces an empty candidate list.
    CLI: ["../cli/cli_package.rq".commands] `analyse --local-symbolic <file>`.
    Sidebar: ["../extension/module/activitybar-panels/current_context_scope.rq".reference_lists_pane]
    merges live same-file inbound/outbound with indexed refs ([local_symbolic_sidebar]).
    Related: ["../language/syntax.rq".open_file_reference_sequencing], [index],
    ["./cache-reuse.rq".unify_inbound_indexes].

    @status done
    @implementation (
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/src/extract.rs"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/src/types.rs"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-napi/src/lib.rs"]
        ["../../packages/analytical/src/native/parse-source.ts"]
        ["../../packages/analytical/src/core/local-symbolic-references.ts"]
        ["../../packages/language/src/reqlan-document-link-provider.ts"]
        ["../../packages/language/src/reqlan-definition-provider.ts"]
        ["../../packages/language/src/reqlan-local-symbolic-links.ts"]
        ["../../packages/cli/src/commands/analyse.ts"]
        ["../../packages/extension/src/activity_bar_module/local-symbolic-context.ts"]
        ["../../packages/extension/src/activity_bar_module/context-model.ts"]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/tests/local_symbolic.rs:analyze_local_symbolic_returns_outbound_without_catalog"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/tests/local_symbolic.rs:analyze_local_symbolic_ignores_catalog_candidates"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/tests/local_symbolic.rs:analyze_local_symbolic_includes_same_file_inbound_backlinks"]
        ["../../packages/analytical/test/load-native.test.ts:exposes analyzeLocalSymbolic on the engine when present"]
        ["../../packages/analytical/test/local-symbolic-references.test.ts"]
        ["../../packages/language/test/local-symbolic-links.test.ts:same-file idea links without DocumentBuilder / workspace link"]
        ["../../packages/cli/test/local-symbolic.test.ts"]
        ["../../packages/extension/test/local-symbolic-context.test.ts"]
    )
}

local_symbolic_sidebar {
    The activity bar reference lists and current-file scope must consume [local_symbolic_analysis]
    for the open buffer text so same-file inbound backlinks and outbound refs appear even when
    the SQLite index is stale or not ready.
    Merge live local rows with indexed `listReferencesForIdea` / hop-depth rows; dedupe by
    direction plus edge id (and by idea id for scope idea chips).
    Prefer the referencer name as the inbound label (not the edge target label).
    @status done
    @implementation (
        ["../../packages/extension/src/activity_bar_module/local-symbolic-context.ts"]
        ["../../packages/extension/src/activity_bar_module/context-model.ts"]
        ["../../packages/extension/src/activity_bar_module/context-helpers.ts"]
        ["../../packages/analytical/src/index-store/sqlite-store.ts"]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../packages/extension/test/local-symbolic-context.test.ts"]
        ["../../packages/extension/test/context-model.test.ts"]
    )
}

ownership {
    The [index] / indexer lives in `packages/analytical` (`@reqlan/analytical`).
    Canonical single-base engine: [workspace_index] (`WorkspaceIndex` facade).
    Sync/idle impl: [workspace_index_sync]; one-file parse+persist: [workspace_index_file]; mtime stale diff: [workspace_mtime].
    Multi-base registry: one `WorkspaceIndex` per discovered ["../bases/base.rq".base] under [app_memory_doc.application_memory] (`<base>/.reqlan/`).
    Headless entry: [analysis_runtime] via native-only `openAnalysisApi` (CLI / MCP).
    On-disk store path: [application_memory_impl] under `<base>/.reqlan/` — see [app_memory_doc.application_memory].
}

consumption {
    Consumers of the analytical [index]:
    - [extension] — thin VS Code adapter [editor_index_adapter] (file watchers, Uri conversion, UI status)
    - CLI (`["../cli/cli_package.rq".cli_package]`) and MCP — headless [analysis_runtime]
    The extension does not own the indexing engine; it only hosts the adapter.
    Module map: [consumers.index_consumers].
}

nonblocking_index {
    Index sync must stay non-blocking for the host UI (notably [activity_bar_doc.activity_bar] and [workspace_pane_doc.workspace_loading]).
    Editor startup is gated by ["../extension/activation.rq".first_paint_startup]; discovering a base must not construct Langium services, which are initialized lazily on the first parse.
    While syncing, surface progress — state, processed/total, and the current file — in [workspace_pane_doc.workspace_pane] and [ideas_summary_doc.index_panel].
    In-flight sync must be cancellable from those surfaces; cancel keeps already-indexed rows and returns the index to ready.
    Incremental behaviour (see also [graph_analysers.indexing_incrementality]):
    - Single-file create/change/delete via watchers indexes only that file — never a full base walk.
    - Soft full sync (`syncWorkspace` / Refresh) skips parse+persist when the file's mtime matches the value stored on the documents row.
    - Hard refresh (`clearAndRebuildIndex` / Clear & rebuild) wipes the store and reindexes every file.
    Implemented by [workspace_index]; editor adapter [editor_index_adapter].
    @tests (
        [workspace_index_tests]
        ["../../packages/analytical/src/index-store/workspace-index.ts"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/tests/sync.rs:soft_sync_skips_unchanged_mtime"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/tests/sync.rs:hard_rebuild_reindexes_despite_mtime"]
    )
    @status done
}

triggers {
    Index refresh behaviour (capability detail in [graph_analysers]):
    - [graph_analysers.indexing_incrementality] / [nonblocking_index] — incremental where possible
    - [graph_analysers.indexing_trigger_filesave] / [app_memory_doc.idea_index_triggers] — on `.rq` or indexed code-file change
    - [graph_analysers.indexing_trigger_manual] — manual reindex commands
    - [graph_analysers.indexing_trigger_open] — one soft sync after the activity-bar first-paint gate
    - [graph_analysers.indexing_trigger_auto] — idle background mtime staleness check (cheap; not a full reindex)
    Editor watches + idle scheduler: [editor_index_adapter]; headless syncs on runtime activate.
    Full sequence: [sequencing.index_sequencing].
}

capabilities {
    Product capabilities over the [index]: [graph_analysers.index_ideas], [graph_analysers.index_technology], and sibling analysers in that file.
    Indexing performance timing and diagnostic UI: ["../extension/features-index-diagnostics.rq".index_diagnostics].
}

index_diagnostics_timing {
    Soft sync and per-file index paths record durations into the diagnostic index under [app_memory_doc.index_diagnostics_store].
    See ["../extension/features-index-diagnostics.rq".index_diagnostics_metrics].
    Must not block [nonblocking_index]; recording failures are swallowed / logged by the store and must not fail the sync.
}


index_code_files {
    Index non-`.rq` source files that contain [comment_reference] (`rq:[idea]` / `rq:["path".idea]`).
    After the `.rq` pass, the native sync walks allowlisted text files (respecting `.rqignore`, [app_memory_doc.binary_ignore], and nested child bases).
    Binary files stay out unless a negation such as `!*.bin` opts them in.
    The walk cheap-filters on `rq:`, and persists matching files as documents plus `comment_link` edges.
    Edge shape: source = referenced idea, `target_file` = code file URI, kind `comment_link` (no synthetic file ideas).
    Reindex of a `.rq` file re-applies comment links from already-indexed code documents so FK cascade does not drop them.
    Watcher + idle stale check cover code documents as well as `.rq` files ([triggers], [nonblocking_index]).
    Consumers: [graph_analysers.file_related_requirements], ["../core_analysis/search.rq".file_search],
    ["../core_analysis/html_export.rq".html_export_code_reference_pages], Ideas Summary comment-reference rows,
    local graph (idea → external file node), ["../cli/click.rq".click_code_file].
    See [graph_analysers.index_comment_reference_inclusion], ["../ontology.rq".referenced_files].
    @status done
    @implementation (
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/src/comment.rs"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/src/sync.rs"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/src/store.rs"]
        ["../../packages/extension/src/analytical_submodule/index-store/index-service.ts"]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/tests/code_file_index.rs:indexes_comment_references_from_non_rq_files"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/tests/code_file_index.rs:unqualified_comment_ref_matches_catalog_idea_name"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/tests/code_file_index.rs:rq_reindex_restores_comment_links"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/tests/code_file_index.rs:skips_binary_comment_files_unless_rqignore_negation"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-analytical/tests/file_context.rs:file_context_includes_indexed_comment_links"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-analytical/tests/fuzzy_search.rs:workspace_index_fuzzy_search_includes_comment_code_files"]
    )
}



indexer_rust {
    The [index] engine (parse-for-index → extract → SQLite persist → incremental sync) should be written in Rust.
    Crate: `reqlan-index` over `reqlan-parse` per ["../core_analysis/rust_port.rq".rust_crate_layout].
    Extractor ports ["../../crates/reqlan-index/src/extract.rs"] including [wildcard_reference_edges].
    Store ports schema v4 (["../../packages/analytical/src/index-store/schema.ts"]) via rusqlite; diagnostics live in `index-diagnostics.sqlite` on the same engine.
    Sync keeps [nonblocking_index]: per-file upsert, mtime skip, hard rebuild, cancellable progress.
    Not the Langium LSP. Comment-file indexing: [index_code_files].
    @status in-progress
    @todo surface per-file timing diagnostics from Rust sync into IndexDiagnosticsStore
    @tests (
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/tests/extract_parity.rs:indexes_scalar_list_block_and_flag_attribute_values"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/tests/extract_parity.rs:qualified_ideaset_member_reference_targets_leaf_idea_not_ideaset"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/tests/golden_corpus.rs:corpus_idea_names_match_langium_extract"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/tests/schema.rs:opens_at_schema_version_4"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/tests/sync.rs:soft_sync_skips_unchanged_mtime"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/tests/wildcard_reference_edges.rs:expands_wildcard_refs_to_one_edge_per_matching_idea"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/tests/wildcard_reference_edges.rs:sync_persists_wildcard_reference_edges"]
    )
    @plan {
        goal
            Native WorkspaceIndex: same rows and incremental behaviour, no Langium on the index path.

        constraints
            - Schema v4 rusqlite only (no sql.js fallback) after ["../core_analysis/rust_port.rq".cutover].
            - [nonblocking_index] and [index_diagnostics_timing] still apply.
            - Wildcard fan-out stays [wildcard_reference_edges].
            - Extension requires the host-matching core engine `.node` from the per-target VSIX.

        steps
            1. Rust AST → IdeaRecord / EdgeRecord parity tests against the current extractor.
            2. rusqlite store + migrations matching SCHEMA_VERSION 4.
            3. Soft/hard sync, mtime skip, cancel, diagnostics.
            4. Wire through ["../core_analysis/rust_port.rq".native_bridge] once parse+extract golden tests pass.

        open
            - Richer per-file timing rows from Rust sync into the diagnostics store.
    }
}